# LinguaFlow — Translator

A clean, dark-themed translation web app powered by the **MyMemory Translation API** and the browser's **Web Speech API**. No backend, no API key, no build step — just open `index.html` and go.

---

## Features

- **100+ languages** — translate between 40+ languages including English, Arabic, Urdu, Chinese, Hindi, Japanese, and more
- **Free translation** via the [MyMemory API](https://mymemory.translated.net/) — no key required
- **Text-to-Speech** — listen to both the source text and the translated output using the browser's built-in Speech Synthesis
- **Swap languages** — instantly swap source and target languages, with optional text carry-over
- **Use as input** — send the translated result back as new source text for chained translations
- **Copy to clipboard** — one-click copy of the translated output
- **Match quality indicator** — shows a confidence percentage returned by the API
- **Character limit** — supports up to 5,000 characters with a live counter and warning at 4,500
- **Keyboard shortcut** — `Ctrl+Enter` / `Cmd+Enter` to trigger translation
- **Responsive layout** — two-panel side-by-side view on desktop, stacked on mobile

---

## Getting Started

No installation or dependencies required.

```bash
# Just open the file in any modern browser
open index.html
```

Or serve it locally:

```bash
npx serve .
# or
python -m http.server 8080
```

Then visit `http://localhost:8080`.

---

## Usage

1. Select a **source language** from the left dropdown (default: English)
2. Select a **target language** from the right dropdown (default: Urdu)
3. Type or paste text into the **Source Text** panel
4. Click **Translate** or press `Ctrl+Enter`
5. The translation appears in the right panel

### Additional Actions

| Button | Action |
|---|---|
| 🔊 (source) | Read source text aloud |
| 🔊 (target) | Read translated text aloud |
| ⇅ Swap | Swap source and target languages |
| Copy | Copy translation to clipboard |
| Use as input → | Move translation back to source for re-translation |
| ✕ Clear | Clear source text and reset output |

---

## Tech Stack

| Concern | Technology |
|---|---|
| Translation | [MyMemory API](https://mymemory.translated.net/) (free, no key) |
| Text-to-Speech | Web Speech API (`SpeechSynthesisUtterance`) |
| Fonts | Google Fonts — DM Serif Display, DM Sans |
| Styling | Vanilla CSS with custom properties |
| Logic | Vanilla JavaScript (ES2020+) |

No frameworks, no build tools, no dependencies.

---

## Browser Support

Works in all modern browsers. Text-to-Speech requires a browser that supports the [Web Speech API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web_Speech_API) (Chrome, Edge, Safari, Firefox 49+). The app degrades gracefully — TTS buttons are disabled if unsupported.

---

## API Notes

- The **MyMemory free tier** allows ~1,000 requests/day per IP
- No API key is needed for basic usage
- For higher limits, register at [mymemory.translated.net](https://mymemory.translated.net/) and append `&de=youremail@example.com` to the request URL in the source

